TEST 5  KiDS BUDGET (CFG24/CFG27: cost in delta-chi2 of the cold budget's edge vs KiDS's own best)
======================================================================================================================
  committed: smallest standard-halo spread S = 50.2 in delta-chi2 [campaign_fresh_gravity/CFG27_edge_thread_closure.out:33]; budget costs {'canonical P2': 29.4, 'canonical nu_mono': 32.9, 'alt P2': 45.4, 'alt nu_mono': 49.3} [campaign_fresh_gravity/CFG27_edge_thread_closure.out:34, campaign_fresh_gravity/CFG27_edge_thread_closure.out:37].
  cost/S = canonical P2 0.59, canonical nu_mono 0.66, alt P2 0.90, alt nu_mono 0.98
  Both cost and S are delta-chi2 between fixed models, so both grow in proportion to survey area: the ratio is INVARIANT to N.  No survey size moves cost above S;
  only a better standard-halo model (smaller S) could.  The B-vs-NFW difference is 104.7 - 99.3 = 5.4 [campaign_fresh_gravity/CFG23_README.md:38], which is 0.11 of S.
  => KiDS: not forecastable from committed budgets as an N or precision requirement; capped by the machinery spread, not by statistics.
  (MUTATE: machinery spread S set to 0 -> every cost would exceed it, an 'exclusion' at any N: the headline changes)

